    "change_rationale": "Prior 90/5/5 mixture was ~10x lower in replay than every published recipe that succeeded at target-language CPT. Typhoon 2 (Thai, 1B-70B) used 50 percent English explicitly citing catastrophic-forgetting mitigation; Racka (Hungarian, academic HPC) used ~56 percent non-target (24 EN + 21 DE + 11 code); EstLLM used English replay plus code, math and instruction-like data. At 1-2B capacity the forgetting risk is higher than at larger scale, so a 90 percent target-language mixture risks a model that gains little Thai while losing English and reasoning.",
